This is a C++/CUDA project for medical imaging and pose optimization with the following key components:

- Core library (libjtml_core.a): Handles basic data structures, optimization, and machine learning
- GPU library (libjtml_gpu.so): CUDA-based implementations for image processing and DRR rendering
- Cost Functions library (libJTA_Cost_Functions.so): Various optimization metrics and constraints
- Qt-based GUI: Main interface with visualization tools

Build Environment:
- Managed via pixi.toml for dependencies
- CMake-based build system
- CUDA toolkit and Qt6 dependencies
- C++17 standard

Key Areas:
- Optimization algorithms: DIRECT/Dividing rectangles implementation
- CUDA kernels: DRR rendering, image processing, metrics
- Cost functions: Different optimization strategies and constraints

Code Style Guidelines:
- Use camelCase for method names
- Use PascalCase for class names
- Maintain consistent 4-space indentation
- Group related functions together
- Document complex CUDA kernels and optimization algorithms

Critical Files:
- src/core/*: Core optimization algorithms
- src/gpu/*.cu: CUDA kernel implementations
- src/cost_functions/*: Optimization metrics

Important Directories:
- src/core: Core algorithms and data structures
- src/gpu: CUDA implementations
- src/gui: Qt-based interface
- src/cost_functions: Optimization metrics
- include/*: Header files matching source structure

Testing Requirements:
- Any new CUDA kernel should have CPU validation
- GUI changes should maintain existing workflow
- Optimization changes need convergence verification

Please confirm before:
- Modifying optimization algorithms
- Changing CUDA kernel implementations
- Making structural changes to core components
